---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Mirrors the in-app Privacy Policy (SettingsView.swift). Keep the two in sync.
const contactEmail = 'support@pumpdeck.app';
const lastUpdated = 'May 6, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — PumpDeck"
  description="How PumpDeck handles your data."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-600">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-soft">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div
      class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-ink-soft [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:text-ink [&_a]:text-brand-600 [&_a]:underline"
    >
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <p>
          This document describes how PumpDeck ("the app", "we") handles your
          data. It will be reviewed by counsel before final App Store
          submission; the structure and commitments below are what we plan to
          publish.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          You sign in with Apple or Google. Through that we receive your email
          address (or Apple's private relay address) — we never ask for or store
          a password.
        </p>
        <p>
          When you use the app, you may add: a chosen display name, body weight
          and height, body measurements, progress photos, and your full workout
          history (exercises, sets, weights, reps, plans, templates, notes).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>2. How it is stored</h2>
        <p>
          Your account and the data you create are stored in our database hosted
          on Supabase (US region). Data is transmitted over TLS and stored
          encrypted at rest. Photos and exercise media are stored in object
          storage with the same protections.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>3. Who sees it</h2>
        <p>
          Your data is yours. We do not sell it, share it with advertisers, or
          use it to train any model. The only third party with technical access
          to it is our infrastructure provider (Supabase), who acts as a data
          processor under their published terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not include any third-party analytics, tracking, or advertising
          SDKs in the app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>4. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can export your data at any time from Settings → Data → Export.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can delete your account and every record we hold about you from
          Settings → Account → Delete account &amp; all data. This is immediate
          and permanent.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you live in a region with formal data rights (GDPR, CCPA, etc.),
          you can also email us to exercise them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>5. Children</h2>
        <p>
          PumpDeck is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly
          collect data from them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>6. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If we materially change how we handle your data, we will update this
          document and notify you in-app the next time you launch.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2>7. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
